.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
.Dd July 23, 2026
.Dt EMACS-JOURNAL-2026-07-23 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-journal-2026-07-23
.Nd working notes of 2026-07-23
.Sh ENTRIES
.Ss Fix Jinx: No dictionaries available for \(dqen_US\(dq — bundle aspell dicts
.Ss Summary
Resolved the jinx spell-check error deferred on 2026-06-09 and 2026-07-20 as a \(dqdeployment gap.\(dq
The distribution now bundles its aspell dictionaries, so
.Ql "just run-built" ,
.Ql "just screenshot" ,
and every module consumer spell-check out of the box.
.Ss Corrected root cause
The earlier notes were wrong on two counts, verified against the pinned nixpkgs:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fBenchant \fIdoes\fP have the aspell backend.\fP
.Ql "enchant-2.6.9"
is built with
.Ql "--with-aspell"
(aspell sits in
.Ql "propagatedBuildInputs" ),
alongside hunspell/nuspell/voikko.
There was never a missing-backend problem.
.It
\fBThe distribution shipped no dictionary data.\fP
.Ql "jotainEmacsPackages*"
.No \&( Ns Ql "nix/mk-overlay.nix" )
pulled in the enchant + aspell \fIlibraries\fP via the
.Ql "jinx"
epkg, but nothing added an
.Ql "aspell-dict-*"
package to the closure. jinx's C module therefore loaded, enchant initialised, and libaspell found no
.Ql "en_US"
dictionary anywhere → the error.
.El
.Pp
The modules install
.Ql "pkgs.aspellDicts.en"
into a profile and rely on nixpkgs' libaspell
.Ql "data-dirs-from-nix-profiles.patch"
to find
.Ql "$NIX_PROFILES/*/lib/aspell"
at runtime.
That works only when
.Ql "NIX_PROFILES"
is populated at launch — so a bare
.Ql "./result/bin/emacs"
(the
.Ql "just run-built"
path) or a systemd/launchd daemon with an empty
.Ql "NIX_PROFILES"
still failed.
.Ss Why NIX_PROFILES is not enough (the trap the modules fell into)
nixpkgs' libaspell
.Ql "data-dirs-from-nix-profiles.patch"
feeds
.Ql "$NIX_PROFILES/*/lib/aspell"
into libaspell's data-dir list \fIonly\fP for dictionary \fBenumeration\fP.
So
.Ql "enchant_broker_list_dicts"
(and
.Ql "enchant-lsmod-2 -list-dicts" )
happily report
.Ql "en_GB (aspell)"
when an
.Ql "aspellDicts.en"
is on
.Ql "NIX_PROFILES"
— but
.Ql "enchant_broker_request_dict" ,
the call jinx actually makes, builds a \fIspeller\fP, whose master word list resolves under the default
.Ql "data-dir"
.No \&( Ns Ql "${aspell}/lib/aspell/en" ,
which does not exist).
Result: enumeration passes, the speller fails, jinx still shows \(dqNo dictionaries available.\(dq
Verified directly:
.Ql "enchant-2 -d en_GB -l"
with only
.Ql "NIX_PROFILES"
set →
.Ql "The file \(dq…/aspell-0.60.8.2/lib/aspell/en\(dq can not be opened for reading" .
This means the modules' profile-installed
.Ql "aspellDicts.en"
never actually worked for spell-checking either — only for the dict list.
.Ss Changes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "nix/mk-overlay.nix" Ns No "\fP"
— build one
.Ql "aspellWithDicts (d: [en fi de fr])"
directory (libaspell data files + all four dicts under a single
.Ql "lib/aspell" )
and, in the
.Ql "mkJotainEmacsPackages"
re-wrap loop, set
.Ql "ASPELL_CONF=\(dqdict-dir <env>/lib/aspell; data-dir <env>/lib/aspell\(dq"
via
.Ql "makeBinaryWrapper --set-default" .
Pointing both
.Ql "dict-dir"
and
.Ql "data-dir"
at the combined directory is what makes
.Ql "request_dict"
succeed.
Verified:
.Ql "enchant-2 -d en_GB -l"
accepts \(dqcolour\(dq, flags \(dqhelllo\(dq; and inside the wrapped Emacs
.Ql "jinx--mod-dict"
returns non-nil for en_GB/fi/de/fr.
.Ql "--set-default"
lets a user (or a module wrapper) still override
.Ql "ASPELL_CONF"
to add languages.
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "lisp/init-writing.el" Ns No "\fP"
— set
.Ql "jinx-languages"
to
.Ql "\(dqen_GB\(dq"
(British English) as the default. fi/de/fr are bundled and reachable per buffer via
.Ql "C-M-$" ;
a single default avoids foreign words silently passing as correct English.
.El
.Ss Notes
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
One edit covers all three distribution builds
.No \&( Ns Ql "jotainEmacsPackages" ,
.Ql "jotainEmacsPackagesNoGui" ,
.Ql "jylhisEmacsPackages" )
— they share the re-wrap loop.
Module consumers
.No \&( Ns Ql "module.nix" ,
.Ql "module-system.nix" ,
.Ql "module-nix-on-droid.nix" )
exec this same wrapped binary without setting
.Ql "ASPELL_CONF" ,
so the
.Ql "--set-default"
applies and they get working spell-check for the four languages with no module change.
.It
Cache parity is untouched: the change lives in the custom
.Ql "jotainEmacsPackages"
derivation, not
.Ql "emacs.nix" ,
so the bare-Emacs store-path parity invariant is unaffected.
.It
\fBFollow-up:\fP the modules'
.Ql "services.jotain.spell.dictionaries"
option and the hardcoded
.Ql "aspellDicts.en"
in
.Ql "module-system.nix"
/
.Ql "module-nix-on-droid.nix"
(and the \(dqlibaspell finds
.Ql "$profile/lib/aspell" Ns No "\(dq"
comments) are now known to be no-ops for actual spell-checking.
To make extra languages configurable, a later change should build an
.Ql "aspellWithDicts"
from that option and export
.Ql "ASPELL_CONF"
in the module wrappers, replacing the profile install.
.El
